CODEGEN.md §2.11, §3.5, DECISIONS 435: a data-mode cpp emit may cut a class's detail::Decode into <P>Access::Decode<N> parts; a record Decode3 is the type the part Decode3 would hide inside the access struct, whatever the record's width.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// Named like a part of Decode.
record Decode3 {
  /// Its size.
  n: Int
}

/// The rows.
let rows: [Decode3] keyed by n = [{ n: 1 }]

emit cpp { out: "@features/a", namespace: "a", mode: data }
emit json { out: "out/" }
-- a.rows.json --
[{ "n": 1 }]
-- findings.txt --
error[E8005]  a/a.canon:4:8
  cpp: Decode3 is generated for both a.Decode3 and a; rename one of them with @cpp(name:)

